# Database Standards

## Prisma Client
- Always use the singleton from `@/lib/db` (`import { db } from "@/lib/db"`).
- Use `include` sparingly — only fetch relations you actually need.
- For list queries, always paginate. Default: 20 items per page.
- Use transactions (`db.$transaction`) for multi-table operations.

## Multi-file Schema (Prisma 6.4+)
- Schema lives under `prisma/schema/` (not a single file). Domain-aligned:
  - `00-base.prisma`     — generator, datasource, enums
  - `10-identity.prisma` — User, Account, Session, Subscription
  - `20-foundation.prisma` — YearlyPlan, WheelOfLifeEntry, AntiGoal, **Area**, **Vision**, **VisionItem**
  - `30-projects.prisma` — **Project** (was Goal), Checkpoint, KeyResult, Motivation
  - `40-execution.prisma` — **Task** (was Action), **System** (was DailySystem), SystemCompletion
  - `50-rhythm.prisma`   — WeeklyPlan, WeeklyCheckIn, **ProjectCheckIn**, MonthlyReview, QuarterlyReview
  - `60-knowledge.prisma` — **Note**, **Resource** (polymorphic via `parentType + parentId`)
  - `70-system.prisma`   — Streak, Achievement, **Drift** (quick-capture inbox), **DailyState**
- Config lives in `prisma.config.ts` (not `package.json`). It points Prisma at the schema folder and seed script.

## PARA Model Terminology (Phase 2+)
- `Area` (life domain) → `Project` (concrete outcome) → `Task` (work unit). `Resource` and `Note` attach to any PARA entity via polymorphic `(parentType, parentId)`.
- Code uses new names: `db.project`, `db.task`, `db.system`, `db.projectCheckIn`, `db.projectCheckpoint`.
- Underlying tables keep legacy names via `@@map` until Phase 7 cleanup (`goals`, `actions`, `daily_systems`, etc.). Do not rename DB columns/tables casually.
- Polymorphic parents on `Note` / `Resource` use the `ParentType` enum: `AREA | PROJECT | TASK | SYSTEM | VISION | VISION_ITEM`.

## Plan Tier Limits (enforce in API routes)
- Source of truth: `planLimits` in `@/lib/config`.
- FREE: 1 yearly plan, 3 projects/plan, 3 tasks/project, 3 systems/project, 6 default Areas (no custom), 12 vision items, 50 notes, 10 link-only resources, no file uploads, lite Wrapped.
- PRO: unlimited plans/projects/tasks/systems, custom Areas, unlimited vision items/notes, 200 resources (link or file), 25 MB/file, 2 GB total, full Wrapped.
- Check limits **before** creating records. Reject with 402 + upgrade message.

## Schema Conventions
- Table names: snake_case plural (`@@map`)
- Column names: camelCase (Prisma convention)
- Always include `createdAt` / `updatedAt` on mutable models
- Use `@default(cuid())` for IDs
- Use enums for fixed-value columns
- Polymorphic relations: pair `parentType` (enum) + `parentId` (String) + a composite index

## Migrations
- Use `prisma migrate dev --create-only` then commit + `prisma migrate deploy`. Never use `db push` against `main`/production.
- Data-seed inserts (e.g. default Areas, Vision row, legacy data copies) live at the end of the same migration file under a clearly-commented section.
- Migration history started fresh in Phase 2 (`00000000000000_baseline` + `20260514000000_para_foundation`); older standalone migrations were folded into baseline.

## Query Patterns
- Use `findUnique` when you have a unique identifier.
- Use `findFirst` with a `where` clause for filtered queries.
- Use `findMany` with `take` and `skip` for paginated lists.
- Always order results explicitly.
- Prefer the helpers in `src/lib/queries/*` over ad-hoc `db.*` calls in pages/components.
